/-!
# The C⋆-envelope of an operator system

A unital complete order embedding `κ : V → E` of an operator system `V` into a unital C⋆-algebra `E`
is a **C⋆-envelope** of `V` (`OperatorSystem.IsCStarEnvelope`) when `κ(V)` generates `E` and every
unital complete order embedding `j : V → A` into a unital C⋆-algebra generated by `j(V)` factors
through a surjective ⋆-homomorphism `π : A → E` with `π ∘ j = κ`. The definition asks this for `A`
in the universe of `V`, and it follows for `A` in any universe
(`OperatorSystem.IsCStarEnvelope.exists_surjective_starAlgHom`), with `π` unique
(`OperatorSystem.IsCStarEnvelope.existsUnique_starAlgHom`). Two C⋆-envelopes of `V` are
⋆-isomorphic over `V` (`OperatorSystem.IsCStarEnvelope.exists_starAlgEquiv`), since `V` generates
them (`OperatorSystem.IsCStarEnvelope.starAlgHom_ext`), and the operator systems that come from
unital C⋆-algebras are exactly those whose C⋆-envelope `κ` is onto
(`OperatorSystem.IsCStarEnvelope.surjective_iff`).

Every operator system `V` has a C⋆-envelope `OperatorSystem.CStarEnvelope V`
(`OperatorSystem.isCStarEnvelope_toCStarEnvelope`), built in its injective envelope. Let `S` be an
operator subsystem of `B(H)` and `φ` a minimal completely positive map on `B(H)` fixing `S`
(`OperatorSubsystem.FixingMap.exists_isMin`), whose range is the injective envelope `I(S)` of `S`.
The map `φ` is an idempotent Schwarz map, so the Choi–Effros product makes its range a unital
C⋆-algebra `ChoiEffros φ.toSchwarzMap`, whose matrix orders are those of `B(H)`
(`ChoiEffros.isCompleteOrderEmbedding_valₗ_iff`). The C⋆-subalgebra generated by `S` in it
(`OperatorSubsystem.FixingMap.cstarEnvelope`) contains `S` as an operator subsystem
(`OperatorSubsystem.FixingMap.isCompleteOrderEmbedding_toCStarEnvelope`) and is generated by it.

It has the universal property (`OperatorSubsystem.FixingMap.exists_starAlgHom`): for every unital
complete order embedding `j` of `S` into a unital C⋆-algebra `A` generated by `j(S)`, in any
universe, there is a unital ⋆-homomorphism from `A` onto it that sends `j s` to `s`. The proof
represents `A` faithfully on a Hilbert space `K`, extends in both directions between `B(K)` and the
injective envelope by injectivity, and uses the rigidity of the injective envelope to see that the
extensions compose to the identity; the equality case of the Kadison–Schwarz inequality then makes
the extension `Ψ : B(K) → I(S)` multiplicative on `A`. The range of a ⋆-homomorphism between
C⋆-algebras is closed (`StarAlgHom.isClosed_range`), so the ⋆-homomorphism is onto. So the inclusion
of `S` is a C⋆-envelope of `S` (`OperatorSubsystem.FixingMap.isCStarEnvelope_toCStarEnvelope`), and
an operator system `V`, embedded in `B(H)` by the Choi–Effros theorem
(`OperatorSystem.isCompleteOrderEmbedding_directSumMap`), has the C⋆-envelope of its image. When `S`
comes from a unital C⋆-algebra `A`, the ⋆-homomorphism is a ⋆-isomorphism
(`OperatorSubsystem.FixingMap.exists_starAlgEquiv`).

Minimality enters as a `Fact` instance, as in `QuantumSystem.Analysis.OperatorSystem.InjectiveEnvelope`,
so that the idempotence of `φ.toSchwarzMap`, which the C⋆-algebra structure of `ChoiEffros` takes as
an instance, is found by instance search.

## Main definitions

* `OperatorSystem.IsCStarEnvelope κ` — `κ : V → E` is a C⋆-envelope of the operator system `V`.
* `OperatorSystem.CStarEnvelope V`, with the scoped notation `C⋆ₑ(V)`,
  `OperatorSystem.toCStarEnvelope V` — the C⋆-envelope of an
  operator system `V` and the embedding of `V` into it.
* `OperatorSubsystem.FixingMap.toSchwarzMap φ` — a map fixing `S` as a Schwarz map.
* `OperatorSubsystem.FixingMap.toChoiEffros φ` — the inclusion of `S` into the Choi–Effros
  C⋆-algebra on the range of `φ`.
* `OperatorSubsystem.FixingMap.cstarEnvelope φ` — the C⋆-envelope of `S`, for minimal `φ`.
* `OperatorSubsystem.FixingMap.toCStarEnvelope φ` — the inclusion of `S` into it.

## Main results

* **`OperatorSystem.isCStarEnvelope_toCStarEnvelope`** — every operator system has a C⋆-envelope.
* **`OperatorSystem.IsCStarEnvelope.exists_surjective_starAlgHom`**,
  `OperatorSystem.IsCStarEnvelope.existsUnique_starAlgHom` — the universal property, for C⋆-algebras
  in any universe, with a unique ⋆-homomorphism.
* **`OperatorSystem.IsCStarEnvelope.exists_starAlgEquiv`** — uniqueness of the C⋆-envelope.
* **`OperatorSystem.IsCStarEnvelope.surjective_iff`** — the operator systems that come from unital
  C⋆-algebras are exactly those that coincide with their C⋆-envelope.
* `OperatorSubsystem.FixingMap.isCompleteOrderEmbedding_toCStarEnvelope` — `S` is an operator
  subsystem of its C⋆-envelope, which it generates
  (`OperatorSubsystem.FixingMap.topologicalClosure_adjoin_range_toCStarEnvelope`).
* **`OperatorSubsystem.FixingMap.exists_starAlgHom`** — the universal property of the C⋆-envelope
  of an operator subsystem of `B(H)`.
* `OperatorSubsystem.FixingMap.isCStarEnvelope_toCStarEnvelope` — the inclusion of `S` into it is a
  C⋆-envelope of `S`.
* `OperatorSubsystem.FixingMap.exists_starAlgEquiv` — an operator system that comes from a unital
  C⋆-algebra `A` has `A` as its C⋆-envelope.
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open scoped CStarAlgebra

universe u

/-! ### C⋆-envelopes -/

namespace OperatorSystem

/-- A unital complete order embedding `κ : V → E` of an operator system `V` into a unital C⋆-algebra
`E` is a **C⋆-envelope** of `V` when `κ(V)` generates `E` and every unital complete order embedding
`j : V → A` into a unital C⋆-algebra `A` generated by `j(V)` factors through a ⋆-homomorphism
`π : A → E` with `π ∘ j = κ`; such a `π` is onto (`OperatorSystem.IsCStarEnvelope.surjective`) and
unique (`OperatorSystem.IsCStarEnvelope.existsUnique_starAlgHom`). The universal property is asked
for `A` in the universe of `V`; it then holds for `A` in any universe
(`OperatorSystem.IsCStarEnvelope.exists_surjective_starAlgHom`). -/
structure IsCStarEnvelope {V : Type u} [AddCommGroup V] [Module ℂ V] [StarAddMonoid V]
    [StarModule ℂ V] [PartialOrder V] [∀ k, PartialOrder (CStarMatrix (Fin k) (Fin k) V)] [One V]
    [OperatorSystem V] {E : Type*} [CStarAlgebra E] [PartialOrder E] [StarOrderedRing E]
    (κ : V →ₗ[ℂ] E) : Prop where
  /-- The embedding is unital. -/
  map_one : κ 1 = 1
  /-- The embedding is a complete order embedding. -/
  isCompleteOrderEmbedding : κ.IsCompleteOrderEmbedding
  /-- `κ(V)` generates `E` as a C⋆-algebra. -/
  topologicalClosure_adjoin_range : (StarAlgebra.adjoin ℂ (Set.range κ)).topologicalClosure = ⊤
  /-- The universal property: every unital complete order embedding `j` of `V` into a unital
  C⋆-algebra `A` generated by `j(V)`, in the universe of `V`, factors through a ⋆-homomorphism
  `π : A → E`. -/
  exists_starAlgHom (A : Type u) [CStarAlgebra A] [PartialOrder A] [StarOrderedRing A]
    (j : V →ₗ[ℂ] A) : j.IsCompleteOrderEmbedding → j 1 = 1 →
      (StarAlgebra.adjoin ℂ (Set.range j)).topologicalClosure = ⊤ →
        ∃ π : A →⋆ₐ[ℂ] E, ∀ v, π (j v) = κ v

namespace IsCStarEnvelope

variable {V : Type*} [AddCommGroup V] [Module ℂ V] [StarAddMonoid V] [StarModule ℂ V] [PartialOrder V]
  [∀ k, PartialOrder (CStarMatrix (Fin k) (Fin k) V)] [One V] [OperatorSystem V]
  {E : Type*} [CStarAlgebra E] [PartialOrder E] [StarOrderedRing E] {κ : V →ₗ[ℂ] E}

/-- ⋆-homomorphisms out of a C⋆-envelope of `V` agree when they agree on `V`, which generates it. -/
lemma starAlgHom_ext (hκ : IsCStarEnvelope κ) {B : Type*} [CStarAlgebra B]
    {f g : E →⋆ₐ[ℂ] B} (h : ∀ v, f (κ v) = g (κ v)) : f = g :=
  StarAlgHom.ext_of_topologicalClosure_adjoin_eq_top hκ.topologicalClosure_adjoin_range
    (map_continuous f) (map_continuous g) <| by
      rintro _ ⟨v, rfl⟩
      exact h v

/-- A ⋆-homomorphism `π : A → E` with `π ∘ j = κ` is onto: its range is closed
(`StarAlgHom.isClosed_range`) and contains `κ(V)`, which generates `E`. -/
lemma surjective (hκ : IsCStarEnvelope κ) {A : Type*} [CStarAlgebra A] {j : V →ₗ[ℂ] A}
    (π : A →⋆ₐ[ℂ] E) (hπ : ∀ v, π (j v) = κ v) : Function.Surjective π := by
  have h : (⊤ : StarSubalgebra ℂ E) ≤ π.range := by
    rw [← hκ.topologicalClosure_adjoin_range]
    refine StarSubalgebra.topologicalClosure_minimal (StarAlgebra.adjoin_le ?_) π.isClosed_range
    rintro _ ⟨v, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨j v, hπ v⟩
  exact fun y => h trivial

end IsCStarEnvelope

end OperatorSystem

/-! ### The C⋆-envelope of an operator subsystem of `B(H)` -/

namespace OperatorSubsystem.FixingMap

variable {H : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H] [CompleteSpace H]
  {S : OperatorSubsystem (H →L[ℂ] H)} (φ : FixingMap S)

/-- A map fixing `S` as a Schwarz map, so that its range carries the Choi–Effros product. -/
abbrev toSchwarzMap : SchwarzMap (H →L[ℂ] H) (H →L[ℂ] H) :=
  KPositiveMapClass.toSchwarzMap φ.toMap φ.map_one.le

/-- A minimal map fixing `S` is idempotent (`OperatorSubsystem.FixingMap.isIdempotentElem_of_isMin`),
so the Choi–Effros product makes its range a C⋆-algebra. -/
instance [Fact (IsMin φ)] :
    Fact (IsIdempotentElem (φ.toSchwarzMap : (H →L[ℂ] H) →ₗ[ℂ] (H →L[ℂ] H))) :=
  ⟨LinearMap.ext fun x => DFunLike.congr_fun (isIdempotentElem_of_isMin φ).eq x⟩

variable [Fact (IsMin φ)]

/-- The inclusion `s ↦ φ s = s` of `S` into the Choi–Effros C⋆-algebra on the range of `φ`. -/
def toChoiEffros : S →ₗ[ℂ] ChoiEffros φ.toSchwarzMap where
  toFun s := ChoiEffros.ofMap φ.toSchwarzMap s
  map_add' _ _ := ChoiEffros.ext (map_add φ.toSchwarzMap _ _)
  map_smul' _ _ := ChoiEffros.ext (map_smul φ.toSchwarzMap _ _)

/-- The underlying operator of `φ.toChoiEffros s` is `s`. -/
@[simp] lemma val_toChoiEffros_apply (s : S) : (φ.toChoiEffros s).val = s :=
  φ.map_eq_self s s.2

/-- **The C⋆-envelope** of `S`: the C⋆-subalgebra generated by `S` in the injective envelope, the
range of a minimal `φ` fixing `S` with the Choi–Effros product. -/
def cstarEnvelope : StarSubalgebra ℂ (ChoiEffros φ.toSchwarzMap) :=
  (StarAlgebra.adjoin ℂ (Set.range φ.toChoiEffros)).topologicalClosure

/-- The C⋆-envelope is closed, hence a C⋆-algebra (`StarSubalgebra.cstarAlgebra`) whose order is
that of the ambient C⋆-algebra (`Subtype.starOrderedRing`). -/
instance : IsClosed (φ.cstarEnvelope : Set (ChoiEffros φ.toSchwarzMap)) :=
  StarSubalgebra.isClosed_topologicalClosure _

/-- `star` is continuous on the C⋆-envelope, as on the ambient C⋆-algebra. -/
instance : ContinuousStar φ.cstarEnvelope :=
  ⟨continuous_induced_rng.mpr (continuous_star.comp continuous_subtype_val)⟩

/-- The matrix orders of the C⋆-envelope as a unital C⋆-algebra. Instance search finds them at each
size, but not uniformly in the size without this instance; the C⋆-algebra structure is that of
`StarSubalgebra.cstarAlgebra`, as for any unital C⋆-algebra. -/
instance instPartialOrderCStarMatrix (k : ℕ) :
    PartialOrder (CStarMatrix (Fin k) (Fin k) φ.cstarEnvelope) :=
  letI : NonUnitalCStarAlgebra φ.cstarEnvelope := CStarAlgebra.toNonUnitalCStarAlgebra _
  inferInstance

/-- The inclusion of `S` into its C⋆-envelope, `s ↦ φ s = s`. -/
def toCStarEnvelope : S →ₗ[ℂ] φ.cstarEnvelope where
  toFun s := ⟨φ.toChoiEffros s,
    StarSubalgebra.le_topologicalClosure _ (StarAlgebra.subset_adjoin ℂ _ ⟨s, rfl⟩)⟩
  map_add' _ _ := Subtype.ext (map_add φ.toChoiEffros _ _)
  map_smul' _ _ := Subtype.ext (map_smul φ.toChoiEffros _ _)

/-- `φ.toCStarEnvelope s` is `φ.toChoiEffros s` in the Choi–Effros C⋆-algebra. -/
@[simp] lemma coe_toCStarEnvelope_apply (s : S) :
    (φ.toCStarEnvelope s : ChoiEffros φ.toSchwarzMap) = φ.toChoiEffros s :=
  rfl

/-- The inclusion of `S` into its C⋆-envelope is unital. -/
lemma toCStarEnvelope_one : φ.toCStarEnvelope 1 = 1 := Subtype.ext (ChoiEffros.ext rfl)

/-- **`S` lies in its C⋆-envelope as an operator subsystem**: the inclusion is a complete order
embedding. The C⋆-envelope is a C⋆-subalgebra of the Choi–Effros C⋆-algebra, which carries the
matrix orders of `B(H)` (`ChoiEffros.isCompleteOrderEmbedding_valₗ_iff`), and the inclusion of a
C⋆-subalgebra is a complete order embedding
(`NonUnitalStarAlgHom.isCompleteOrderEmbedding_of_injective`). -/
lemma isCompleteOrderEmbedding_toCStarEnvelope : φ.toCStarEnvelope.IsCompleteOrderEmbedding :=
  fun k X => by
    have hsub (Y : CStarMatrix (Fin k) (Fin k) φ.cstarEnvelope) : 0 ≤ Y.map Subtype.val ↔ 0 ≤ Y :=
      NonUnitalStarAlgHom.isCompleteOrderEmbedding_of_injective (StarSubalgebra.subtype φ.cstarEnvelope)
        Subtype.val_injective k Y
    have hval (Z : CStarMatrix (Fin k) (Fin k) (ChoiEffros φ.toSchwarzMap)) :
        0 ≤ Z.map ChoiEffros.val ↔ 0 ≤ Z :=
      ChoiEffros.isCompleteOrderEmbedding_valₗ_iff (φ := φ.toSchwarzMap) |>.mpr
        (fun _ _ hX => φ.toMap.map_cstarMatrix_nonneg hX) k Z
    rw [← hsub, ← hval, show ((X.map φ.toCStarEnvelope).map Subtype.val).map ChoiEffros.val =
      X.map Subtype.val from CStarMatrix.ext fun i j => φ.map_eq_self _ (X i j).2]
    rfl

/-- `S` generates its C⋆-envelope. -/
lemma topologicalClosure_adjoin_range_toCStarEnvelope :
    (StarAlgebra.adjoin ℂ (Set.range φ.toCStarEnvelope)).topologicalClosure = ⊤ := by
  refine eq_top_iff.mpr fun x _ => ?_
  rw [← SetLike.mem_coe, StarSubalgebra.topologicalClosure_coe,
    Topology.IsInducing.subtypeVal.closure_eq_preimage_closure_image, Set.mem_preimage]
  have hx : (x : ChoiEffros φ.toSchwarzMap) ∈
      closure (StarAlgebra.adjoin ℂ (Set.range φ.toChoiEffros) : Set (ChoiEffros φ.toSchwarzMap)) := by
    rw [← StarSubalgebra.topologicalClosure_coe]
    exact x.2
  convert hx using 2
  ext z
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨y, hy, rfl⟩
    induction hy using StarAlgebra.adjoin_induction with
    | mem y hy =>
      obtain ⟨s, rfl⟩ := hy
      exact StarAlgebra.subset_adjoin ℂ _ ⟨s, rfl⟩
    | algebraMap r => exact StarSubalgebra.algebraMap_mem _ r
    | add y₁ y₂ _ _ h₁ h₂ => exact add_mem h₁ h₂
    | mul y₁ y₂ _ _ h₁ h₂ => exact mul_mem h₁ h₂
    | star y _ h => exact star_mem h
  · intro hz
    induction hz using StarAlgebra.adjoin_induction with
    | mem z hz =>
      obtain ⟨s, rfl⟩ := hz
      exact ⟨φ.toCStarEnvelope s, StarAlgebra.subset_adjoin ℂ _ ⟨_, rfl⟩, rfl⟩
    | algebraMap r => exact ⟨algebraMap ℂ _ r, StarSubalgebra.algebraMap_mem _ r, rfl⟩
    | add z₁ z₂ _ _ h₁ h₂ =>
      obtain ⟨y₁, hy₁, rfl⟩ := h₁
      obtain ⟨y₂, hy₂, rfl⟩ := h₂
      exact ⟨y₁ + y₂, add_mem hy₁ hy₂, rfl⟩
    | mul z₁ z₂ _ _ h₁ h₂ =>
      obtain ⟨y₁, hy₁, rfl⟩ := h₁
      obtain ⟨y₂, hy₂, rfl⟩ := h₂
      exact ⟨y₁ * y₂, mul_mem hy₁ hy₂, rfl⟩
    | star z _ h =>
      obtain ⟨y, hy, rfl⟩ := h
      exact ⟨star y, star_mem hy, rfl⟩

/-- **The universal property of the C⋆-envelope.** For a unital complete order embedding `j` of `S`
into a unital C⋆-algebra `A` generated by `j(S)`, there is a unital ⋆-homomorphism `π` from `A` onto
the C⋆-envelope with `π ∘ j` the inclusion of `S`, for `A` in any universe; it is unique
(`OperatorSystem.IsCStarEnvelope.existsUnique_starAlgHom`).

Represent `A` faithfully on a Hilbert space `K` (`GNS.DirectSum.repStarAlgHom`), so that
`ρ : A → B(K)` is a complete order embedding
(`NonUnitalStarAlgHom.isCompleteOrderEmbedding_of_injective`). The injective
envelope extends `j(s) ↦ s` to `Ψ : B(K) → I(S)` (`OperatorSubsystem.FixingMap.injective_range`,
`OperatorSystem.Injective.exists_extension`), Arveson's extension theorem extends `s ↦ j(s)` to
`Γ : I(S) → B(K)` (`LinearMap.IsCompleteOrderEmbedding.exists_extension_completelyPositiveMap`), and
`Ψ ∘ Γ` fixes `S`, so it is the identity (`OperatorSubsystem.FixingMap.eq_id_of_isMin`). In the
Choi–Effros C⋆-algebra on `I(S)`, whose matrix orders are those of `B(H)`
(`ChoiEffros.isCompleteOrderEmbedding_valₗ_iff`), `Ψ` and `Γ` are unital completely positive, hence
Schwarz maps, and the values of `Γ` lie in the multiplicative domain of `Ψ`
(`SchwarzMapClass.apply_mem_multiplicativeDomain_of_rightInverse`). This closed ⋆-subalgebra
contains `ρ(j(S)) = Γ(S)`, hence `ρ(A)`, so `π = Ψ ∘ ρ` is a ⋆-homomorphism. Its range is closed
(`StarAlgHom.isClosed_range`) and contains `S`, and it lies in the closure of the ⋆-algebra generated
by `S`. -/
theorem exists_starAlgHom {A : Type*} [CStarAlgebra A] [PartialOrder A] [StarOrderedRing A]
    (j : S →ₗ[ℂ] A) (hj : j.IsCompleteOrderEmbedding) (hj1 : j 1 = 1)
    (hgen : (StarAlgebra.adjoin ℂ (Set.range j)).topologicalClosure = ⊤) :
    ∃ π : A →⋆ₐ[ℂ] φ.cstarEnvelope, Function.Surjective π ∧ ∀ s : S, π (j s) = φ.toCStarEnvelope s := by
  -- a faithful representation `ρ : A → B(K)`
  let ρ := GNS.DirectSum.repStarAlgHom A
  have hρ := NonUnitalStarAlgHom.isCompleteOrderEmbedding_of_injective ρ
    GNS.DirectSum.repStarAlgHom_injective
  have hj' := hρ.comp hj
  have hj'1 : ((ρ : A →ₗ[ℂ] ((GNS.DirectSum.rep A).H →L[ℂ] (GNS.DirectSum.rep A).H)) ∘ₗ j) 1 = 1 := by
    simp [hj1]
  -- the inclusion `ι : S → I(S)`
  let ι := φ.inclusion
  -- the extensions `Ψ₀ : B(K) → I(S)` and `γ : I(S) → B(K)`
  obtain ⟨Ψ₀, hΨ₀⟩ := (injective_range (isIdempotentElem_of_isMin φ)).exists_extension hj' hj'1 ι
  obtain ⟨γ, hγ⟩ := (isCompleteOrderEmbedding_inclusion φ).exists_extension_completelyPositiveMap
    inclusion_one hj'.toCompletelyPositiveMap'
  have hΨ₀j (s : S) : Ψ₀ (ρ (j s)) = ι s := DFunLike.congr_fun hΨ₀ s
  have hγι (s : S) : γ (ι s) = ρ (j s) := DFunLike.congr_fun hγ s
  have hΨ₀γ : Ψ₀.comp γ = CompletelyPositiveMap'.id _ := eq_id_of_isMin _ fun s => by
    change Ψ₀ (γ (ι s)) = ι s
    rw [hγι, hΨ₀j]
  -- the maps `Ψ`, `Γ` between `B(K)` and the Choi–Effros C⋆-algebra `E` on `I(S)`
  have hval : (ChoiEffros.valₗ φ.toSchwarzMap).IsCompleteOrderEmbedding :=
    ChoiEffros.isCompleteOrderEmbedding_valₗ_iff.mpr fun _ _ hX => φ.toMap.map_cstarMatrix_nonneg hX
  let e₁ : ChoiEffros φ.toSchwarzMap →CP' φ.range :=
    { toLinearMap := LinearMap.codRestrict φ.range.toSubmodule (ChoiEffros.valₗ φ.toSchwarzMap)
        fun x => ⟨x.val, ChoiEffros.map_val x⟩
      map_cstarMatrix_nonneg' := fun k X hX => (hval k X).mpr hX }
  let Ψ' : (_ →L[ℂ] _) →CP ChoiEffros φ.toSchwarzMap :=
    CompletelyPositiveMap.comp (ChoiEffros.ofMapCompletelyPositiveMap φ.toSchwarzMap)
      (CompletelyPositiveMap'.equivCompletelyPositiveMap (φ.range.subtype.comp Ψ₀))
  let Γ' : ChoiEffros φ.toSchwarzMap →CP (_ →L[ℂ] _) :=
    CompletelyPositiveMap'.equivCompletelyPositiveMap (γ.comp e₁)
  have he₁ (s : S) : e₁ (φ.toChoiEffros s) = ι s := Subtype.ext (φ.map_eq_self s s.2)
  have hΓ (s : S) : Γ' (φ.toChoiEffros s) = ρ (j s) := by
    change γ (e₁ _) = _
    rw [he₁, hγι]
  have hΨ (y : _ →L[ℂ] _) : Ψ' y = ChoiEffros.ofMap φ.toSchwarzMap ((Ψ₀ y : φ.range) : H →L[ℂ] H) :=
    rfl
  have hΨ1 : Ψ' 1 = 1 := by
    rw [hΨ, show (1 : _ →L[ℂ] _) = ρ (j 1) by simp [hj1], hΨ₀j]
    exact ChoiEffros.ext rfl
  have hΓ1 : Γ' 1 = 1 := by
    rw [show (1 : ChoiEffros φ.toSchwarzMap) = φ.toChoiEffros 1 from ChoiEffros.ext rfl, hΓ, hj1,
      _root_.map_one]
  let Ψs := KPositiveMapClass.toSchwarzMap Ψ' hΨ1.le
  let Γs := KPositiveMapClass.toSchwarzMap Γ' hΓ1.le
  have hΨΓ : Function.RightInverse Γs Ψs := fun x => by
    change ChoiEffros.ofMap φ.toSchwarzMap ((Ψ₀ (γ (e₁ x)) : φ.range) : H →L[ℂ] H) = x
    rw [show Ψ₀ (γ (e₁ x)) = e₁ x from DFunLike.congr_fun hΨ₀γ (e₁ x)]
    exact ChoiEffros.ofMap_val x
  -- `ρ(A)` lies in the multiplicative domain `M` of `Ψ`
  set M := LinearMap.multiplicativeDomain Ψs
  have hΨc : Continuous Ψs :=
    AddMonoidHomClass.continuous_of_bound Ψs 1 fun x => by simpa using SchwarzMapClass.norm_apply_le Ψs x
  have hMc : IsClosed (M : Set ((GNS.DirectSum.rep A).H →L[ℂ] (GNS.DirectSum.rep A).H)) := by
    have : (M : Set ((GNS.DirectSum.rep A).H →L[ℂ] (GNS.DirectSum.rep A).H)) =
        ⋂ b, ({a | Ψs (a * b) = Ψs a * Ψs b} ∩ {a | Ψs (b * a) = Ψs b * Ψs a}) := by
      ext a
      simp [M, LinearMap.mem_multiplicativeDomain]
    rw [this]
    exact isClosed_iInter fun b =>
      (isClosed_eq (hΨc.comp (continuous_id.mul continuous_const)) (hΨc.mul continuous_const)).inter
        (isClosed_eq (hΨc.comp (continuous_const.mul continuous_id)) (continuous_const.mul hΨc))
  have hjM (s : S) : ρ (j s) ∈ M := by
    rw [← hΓ]
    exact SchwarzMapClass.apply_mem_multiplicativeDomain_of_rightInverse Ψs Γs hΨΓ _
  have hsub : (StarAlgebra.adjoin ℂ (Set.range j) : Set A) ⊆ ρ ⁻¹' M := fun a ha => by
    induction ha using StarAlgebra.adjoin_induction with
    | mem x hx =>
      obtain ⟨s, rfl⟩ := hx
      exact hjM s
    | algebraMap r =>
      change ρ (algebraMap ℂ A r) ∈ M
      rw [AlgHomClass.commutes, Algebra.algebraMap_eq_smul_one]
      exact SMulMemClass.smul_mem r (LinearMap.one_mem_multiplicativeDomain hΨ1)
    | add x y _ _ hx hy =>
      change ρ (x + y) ∈ M
      rw [map_add]
      exact add_mem hx hy
    | mul x y _ _ hx hy =>
      change ρ (x * y) ∈ M
      rw [map_mul]
      exact mul_mem hx hy
    | star x _ hx =>
      change ρ (star x) ∈ M
      rw [map_star]
      exact star_mem hx
  have hcl (a : A) : a ∈ closure (StarAlgebra.adjoin ℂ (Set.range j) : Set A) := by
    rw [← StarSubalgebra.topologicalClosure_coe, hgen]
    trivial
  have hall (a : A) : ρ a ∈ M := closure_minimal hsub (hMc.preimage (map_continuous ρ)) (hcl a)
  -- the ⋆-homomorphism `π₀ = Ψ ∘ ρ` into the Choi–Effros C⋆-algebra
  let π₀ : A →⋆ₐ[ℂ] ChoiEffros φ.toSchwarzMap :=
    { toFun := fun a => Ψs (ρ a)
      map_one' := by
        change Ψ' (ρ 1) = 1
        rw [_root_.map_one, hΨ1]
      map_mul' := fun a b => by
        simp only [map_mul]
        exact (hall a (ρ b)).1
      map_zero' := by simp
      map_add' := fun a b => by simp
      commutes' := fun r => by
        simp only [Algebra.algebraMap_eq_smul_one, map_smul]
        change r • Ψ' (ρ 1) = r • 1
        rw [_root_.map_one, hΨ1]
      map_star' := fun a => by simp [map_star] }
  have hπj (s : S) : π₀ (j s) = φ.toChoiEffros s := by
    change Ψ' (ρ (j s)) = _
    rw [hΨ, hΨ₀j]
    rfl
  have himage : π₀ '' Set.range j = Set.range φ.toChoiEffros := by
    ext x
    constructor
    · rintro ⟨_, ⟨s, rfl⟩, rfl⟩
      exact ⟨s, (hπj s).symm⟩
    · rintro ⟨s, rfl⟩
      exact ⟨j s, ⟨s, rfl⟩, hπj s⟩
  -- its range is the C⋆-envelope
  have hrange : π₀.range = φ.cstarEnvelope := by
    refine le_antisymm ?_ ?_
    · rintro _ ⟨a, rfl⟩
      have hmap : π₀ '' (StarAlgebra.adjoin ℂ (Set.range j) : Set A) ⊆
          StarAlgebra.adjoin ℂ (Set.range φ.toChoiEffros) := by
        rw [← himage, ← StarAlgHom.map_adjoin]
        rintro _ ⟨b, hb, rfl⟩
        exact ⟨b, hb, rfl⟩
      change π₀ a ∈ ((cstarEnvelope φ : StarSubalgebra ℂ _) : Set _)
      rw [cstarEnvelope, StarSubalgebra.topologicalClosure_coe]
      exact closure_mono hmap (image_closure_subset_closure_image (map_continuous π₀) ⟨a, hcl a, rfl⟩)
    · refine StarSubalgebra.topologicalClosure_minimal (StarAlgebra.adjoin_le ?_) ?_
      · rintro _ ⟨s, rfl⟩
        exact ⟨j s, hπj s⟩
      · change IsClosed (Set.range π₀)
        exact π₀.isClosed_range
  refine ⟨π₀.codRestrict _ fun a => hrange ▸ ⟨a, rfl⟩, fun y => ?_, fun s => Subtype.ext (hπj s)⟩
  have hy : (y : ChoiEffros φ.toSchwarzMap) ∈ π₀.range := by
    rw [hrange]
    exact y.2
  obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := hy
  exact ⟨a, Subtype.ext ha⟩

/-- **An operator system that comes from a unital C⋆-algebra coincides with its C⋆-envelope.** If
`j` is a unital complete order isomorphism of `S` onto a unital C⋆-algebra `A`, then the
⋆-homomorphism `π` of `A` onto the C⋆-envelope of `S` of the universal property
(`OperatorSubsystem.FixingMap.exists_starAlgHom`), which sends `j s` to `s`, is a ⋆-isomorphism:
it is injective since `φ` fixes `S`, and onto the C⋆-envelope. -/
lemma exists_starAlgEquiv {A : Type*} [CStarAlgebra A] [PartialOrder A] [StarOrderedRing A]
    (j : S →ₗ[ℂ] A) (hj : j.IsCompleteOrderEmbedding) (hj1 : j 1 = 1)
    (hsurj : Function.Surjective j) :
    ∃ π : A ≃⋆ₐ[ℂ] φ.cstarEnvelope, ∀ s : S, π (j s) = φ.toCStarEnvelope s := by
  have hgen : (StarAlgebra.adjoin ℂ (Set.range j)).topologicalClosure = ⊤ := by
    refine eq_top_iff.mpr fun a _ => StarSubalgebra.le_topologicalClosure _ ?_
    exact StarAlgebra.subset_adjoin ℂ _ (hsurj.range_eq ▸ Set.mem_univ a)
  obtain ⟨π, hπ, hπj⟩ := exists_starAlgHom φ j hj hj1 hgen
  refine ⟨StarAlgEquiv.ofBijective π ⟨fun a b hab => ?_, hπ⟩, hπj⟩
  obtain ⟨s, rfl⟩ := hsurj a
  obtain ⟨t, rfl⟩ := hsurj b
  rw [hπj, hπj] at hab
  have h : (φ.toChoiEffros s).val = (φ.toChoiEffros t).val :=
    congrArg (fun x : φ.cstarEnvelope => (x : ChoiEffros φ.toSchwarzMap).val) hab
  rw [val_toChoiEffros_apply, val_toChoiEffros_apply] at h
  rw [Subtype.ext h]

/-- **The inclusion of `S` into its C⋆-envelope is a C⋆-envelope of `S`**
(`OperatorSystem.IsCStarEnvelope`): it is a unital complete order embedding
(`OperatorSubsystem.FixingMap.isCompleteOrderEmbedding_toCStarEnvelope`), `S` generates
(`OperatorSubsystem.FixingMap.topologicalClosure_adjoin_range_toCStarEnvelope`), and the universal
property holds (`OperatorSubsystem.FixingMap.exists_starAlgHom`). -/
lemma isCStarEnvelope_toCStarEnvelope :
    OperatorSystem.IsCStarEnvelope (V := S) (E := φ.cstarEnvelope) φ.toCStarEnvelope where
  map_one := φ.toCStarEnvelope_one
  isCompleteOrderEmbedding := φ.isCompleteOrderEmbedding_toCStarEnvelope
  topologicalClosure_adjoin_range := φ.topologicalClosure_adjoin_range_toCStarEnvelope
  exists_starAlgHom _ _ _ _ j hj hj1 hgen :=
    let ⟨π, _, hπ⟩ := exists_starAlgHom φ j hj hj1 hgen
    ⟨π, hπ⟩

variable {V : Type*} [AddCommGroup V] [Module ℂ V] [StarAddMonoid V] [StarModule ℂ V] [PartialOrder V]
  [∀ k, PartialOrder (CStarMatrix (Fin k) (Fin k) V)] [One V] [OperatorSystem V]

omit [StarAddMonoid V] [StarModule ℂ V] [PartialOrder V] [OperatorSystem V] in
/-- The universal property of the C⋆-envelope of `S` (`OperatorSubsystem.FixingMap.exists_starAlgHom`),
transported along a unital complete order isomorphism `e : V ≃ S`. -/
theorem exists_starAlgHom_comp (e : V ≃ₗ[ℂ] S) (he : (e : V →ₗ[ℂ] S).IsCompleteOrderEmbedding)
    (he1 : e 1 = 1) {A : Type*} [CStarAlgebra A] [PartialOrder A] [StarOrderedRing A]
    (j : V →ₗ[ℂ] A) (hj : j.IsCompleteOrderEmbedding) (hj1 : j 1 = 1)
    (hgen : (StarAlgebra.adjoin ℂ (Set.range j)).topologicalClosure = ⊤) :
    ∃ π : A →⋆ₐ[ℂ] φ.cstarEnvelope, Function.Surjective π ∧ ∀ v, π (j v) = φ.toCStarEnvelope (e v) := by
  have he1' : e.symm 1 = 1 := e.symm_apply_eq.mpr he1.symm
  obtain ⟨π, hπ, hπj⟩ := exists_starAlgHom φ (j ∘ₗ (e.symm : S →ₗ[ℂ] V)) (hj.comp he.symm)
    (by rw [LinearMap.comp_apply, LinearEquiv.coe_coe, he1', hj1]) (by
      rwa [LinearMap.coe_comp, Set.range_comp, LinearEquiv.coe_coe, e.symm.surjective.range_eq,
        Set.image_univ])
  refine ⟨π, hπ, fun v => ?_⟩
  have h := hπj (e v)
  rwa [LinearMap.comp_apply, LinearEquiv.coe_coe, e.symm_apply_apply] at h

/-- The inclusion of `S` into its C⋆-envelope, composed with a unital complete order isomorphism
`e : V ≃ S`, is a C⋆-envelope of `V`. -/
lemma isCStarEnvelope_comp (e : V ≃ₗ[ℂ] S) (he : (e : V →ₗ[ℂ] S).IsCompleteOrderEmbedding)
    (he1 : e 1 = 1) :
    OperatorSystem.IsCStarEnvelope (E := φ.cstarEnvelope) (φ.toCStarEnvelope ∘ₗ (e : V →ₗ[ℂ] S)) where
  map_one := by rw [LinearMap.comp_apply, LinearEquiv.coe_coe, he1, toCStarEnvelope_one]
  isCompleteOrderEmbedding := (isCompleteOrderEmbedding_toCStarEnvelope φ).comp he
  topologicalClosure_adjoin_range := by
    simpa only [LinearMap.coe_comp, LinearEquiv.coe_coe, e.surjective.range_comp] using
      topologicalClosure_adjoin_range_toCStarEnvelope φ
  exists_starAlgHom _ _ _ _ j hj hj1 hgen :=
    let ⟨π, _, hπ⟩ := exists_starAlgHom_comp φ e he he1 j hj hj1 hgen
    ⟨π, hπ⟩

end OperatorSubsystem.FixingMap

/-! ### The C⋆-envelope of an operator system -/

namespace OperatorSystem

section CStarEnvelope

variable (V : Type*) [AddCommGroup V] [Module ℂ V] [StarAddMonoid V] [StarModule ℂ V] [PartialOrder V]
  [∀ k, PartialOrder (CStarMatrix (Fin k) (Fin k) V)] [One V] [OperatorSystem V]

/-- **The C⋆-envelope** `C⋆ₑ(V)` of an operator system `V`: the C⋆-algebra generated by the image of
`V` in its injective envelope (`OperatorSystem.InjectiveEnvelope`), with the Choi–Effros product.
Unlike `OperatorSystem.InjectiveEnvelope`, it is a `def` with its instances declared below: instance
search through the closed ⋆-subalgebra of the Choi–Effros C⋆-algebra times out on an `abbrev`. -/
def CStarEnvelope : Type _ := (OperatorSubsystem.FixingMap.minimal (rangeDirectSumMap V)).cstarEnvelope

@[inherit_doc] scoped[OperatorSystem] notation "C⋆ₑ(" V ")" => OperatorSystem.CStarEnvelope V

/-- The C⋆-algebra structure of the C⋆-envelope. -/
instance : CStarAlgebra (CStarEnvelope V) :=
  inferInstanceAs (CStarAlgebra (OperatorSubsystem.FixingMap.minimal (rangeDirectSumMap V)).cstarEnvelope)

/-- The order of the C⋆-envelope, that of its C⋆-algebra structure. -/
instance : PartialOrder (CStarEnvelope V) :=
  inferInstanceAs (PartialOrder (OperatorSubsystem.FixingMap.minimal (rangeDirectSumMap V)).cstarEnvelope)

/-- The C⋆-envelope is a star-ordered ring. -/
instance : StarOrderedRing (CStarEnvelope V) :=
  inferInstanceAs (StarOrderedRing (OperatorSubsystem.FixingMap.minimal (rangeDirectSumMap V)).cstarEnvelope)

/-- The embedding of `V` into its C⋆-envelope. -/
def toCStarEnvelope : V →ₗ[ℂ] C⋆ₑ(V) :=
  (OperatorSubsystem.FixingMap.minimal (rangeDirectSumMap V)).toCStarEnvelope ∘ₗ
    (linearEquivRangeDirectSumMap V : V →ₗ[ℂ] rangeDirectSumMap V)

/-- **The universal property of the C⋆-envelope of an operator system**, for C⋆-algebras `A` in any
universe: a unital complete order embedding `j : V → A` with `j(V)` generating `A` factors through a
surjective ⋆-homomorphism `π : A → C⋆ₑ(V)` with `π ∘ j = OperatorSystem.toCStarEnvelope V`. This is
the universal property of the
image `S` of `V` in `B(H)` (`OperatorSubsystem.FixingMap.exists_starAlgHom_comp`). -/
theorem exists_surjective_starAlgHom_toCStarEnvelope {A : Type*} [CStarAlgebra A] [PartialOrder A]
    [StarOrderedRing A] (j : V →ₗ[ℂ] A) (hj : j.IsCompleteOrderEmbedding) (hj1 : j 1 = 1)
    (hgen : (StarAlgebra.adjoin ℂ (Set.range j)).topologicalClosure = ⊤) :
    ∃ π : A →⋆ₐ[ℂ] C⋆ₑ(V), Function.Surjective π ∧ ∀ v, π (j v) = toCStarEnvelope V v :=
  OperatorSubsystem.FixingMap.exists_starAlgHom_comp _ _
    (isCompleteOrderEmbedding_linearEquivRangeDirectSumMap V) (linearEquivRangeDirectSumMap_one V)
    j hj hj1 hgen

/-- **Existence of the C⋆-envelope.** The embedding of an operator system `V` into
`OperatorSystem.CStarEnvelope V` is a C⋆-envelope of `V`
(`OperatorSubsystem.FixingMap.isCStarEnvelope_comp`). -/
theorem isCStarEnvelope_toCStarEnvelope : IsCStarEnvelope (E := C⋆ₑ(V)) (toCStarEnvelope V) :=
  OperatorSubsystem.FixingMap.isCStarEnvelope_comp _ _
    (isCompleteOrderEmbedding_linearEquivRangeDirectSumMap V) (linearEquivRangeDirectSumMap_one V)

end CStarEnvelope

namespace IsCStarEnvelope

variable {V : Type*} [AddCommGroup V] [Module ℂ V] [StarAddMonoid V] [StarModule ℂ V] [PartialOrder V]
  [∀ k, PartialOrder (CStarMatrix (Fin k) (Fin k) V)] [One V] [OperatorSystem V]
  {E : Type*} [CStarAlgebra E] [PartialOrder E] [StarOrderedRing E] {κ : V →ₗ[ℂ] E}

/-- **The universal property of a C⋆-envelope, for C⋆-algebras in any universe.** A unital complete
order embedding `j : V → A` with `j(V)` generating `A` factors through a surjective ⋆-homomorphism
`π : A → E` with `π ∘ j = κ`. The C⋆-envelope `C⋆ₑ(V)` (`OperatorSystem.CStarEnvelope`) lies in the
universe of `V`, so the universal property of `κ` gives `σ : C⋆ₑ(V) → E` over `V`, and
`π = σ ∘ π₀` for `π₀ : A → C⋆ₑ(V)` over `V`
(`OperatorSystem.exists_surjective_starAlgHom_toCStarEnvelope`); it is onto
(`OperatorSystem.IsCStarEnvelope.surjective`). -/
theorem exists_surjective_starAlgHom (hκ : IsCStarEnvelope κ) {A : Type*} [CStarAlgebra A]
    [PartialOrder A] [StarOrderedRing A] (j : V →ₗ[ℂ] A) (hj : j.IsCompleteOrderEmbedding)
    (hj1 : j 1 = 1) (hgen : (StarAlgebra.adjoin ℂ (Set.range j)).topologicalClosure = ⊤) :
    ∃ π : A →⋆ₐ[ℂ] E, Function.Surjective π ∧ ∀ v, π (j v) = κ v := by
  have h₀ := isCStarEnvelope_toCStarEnvelope V
  obtain ⟨σ, hσκ⟩ := hκ.exists_starAlgHom C⋆ₑ(V) (toCStarEnvelope V)
    h₀.isCompleteOrderEmbedding h₀.map_one h₀.topologicalClosure_adjoin_range
  obtain ⟨π₀, -, hπ₀j⟩ := exists_surjective_starAlgHom_toCStarEnvelope V j hj hj1 hgen
  have hπ (v : V) : (σ.comp π₀) (j v) = κ v := by rw [StarAlgHom.comp_apply, hπ₀j, hσκ]
  exact ⟨σ.comp π₀, hκ.surjective _ hπ, hπ⟩

/-- **The ⋆-homomorphism of the universal property is unique.** For a unital complete order
embedding `j : V → A` with `j(V)` generating `A`, in any universe, there is exactly one
⋆-homomorphism `π : A → E` with `π ∘ j = κ` (`OperatorSystem.IsCStarEnvelope.exists_surjective_starAlgHom`),
since ⋆-homomorphisms out of `A` agree when they agree on `j(V)`, which generates `A`. -/
theorem existsUnique_starAlgHom (hκ : IsCStarEnvelope κ) {A : Type*} [CStarAlgebra A]
    [PartialOrder A] [StarOrderedRing A] (j : V →ₗ[ℂ] A) (hj : j.IsCompleteOrderEmbedding)
    (hj1 : j 1 = 1) (hgen : (StarAlgebra.adjoin ℂ (Set.range j)).topologicalClosure = ⊤) :
    ∃! π : A →⋆ₐ[ℂ] E, ∀ v, π (j v) = κ v := by
  obtain ⟨π, -, hπ⟩ := hκ.exists_surjective_starAlgHom j hj hj1 hgen
  refine ⟨π, hπ, fun π' hπ' => ?_⟩
  refine StarAlgHom.ext_of_topologicalClosure_adjoin_eq_top hgen (map_continuous π')
    (map_continuous π) ?_
  rintro _ ⟨v, rfl⟩
  rw [hπ', hπ]

/-- **Uniqueness of the C⋆-envelope.** Two C⋆-envelopes `κ₁ : V → E₁` and `κ₂ : V → E₂` of `V` are
⋆-isomorphic over `V`: the universal property
(`OperatorSystem.IsCStarEnvelope.exists_surjective_starAlgHom`) gives ⋆-homomorphisms between them
over `V`, whose composites are identities since `V` generates
(`OperatorSystem.IsCStarEnvelope.starAlgHom_ext`). -/
theorem exists_starAlgEquiv {E₁ : Type*} [CStarAlgebra E₁] [PartialOrder E₁] [StarOrderedRing E₁]
    {E₂ : Type*} [CStarAlgebra E₂] [PartialOrder E₂] [StarOrderedRing E₂] {κ₁ : V →ₗ[ℂ] E₁}
    {κ₂ : V →ₗ[ℂ] E₂} (h₁ : IsCStarEnvelope κ₁) (h₂ : IsCStarEnvelope κ₂) :
    ∃ e : E₁ ≃⋆ₐ[ℂ] E₂, ∀ v, e (κ₁ v) = κ₂ v := by
  obtain ⟨f, -, hf⟩ := h₂.exists_surjective_starAlgHom κ₁ h₁.isCompleteOrderEmbedding h₁.map_one
    h₁.topologicalClosure_adjoin_range
  obtain ⟨g, -, hg⟩ := h₁.exists_surjective_starAlgHom κ₂ h₂.isCompleteOrderEmbedding h₂.map_one
    h₂.topologicalClosure_adjoin_range
  refine ⟨StarAlgEquiv.ofStarAlgHom f g ?_ ?_, hf⟩
  · exact h₁.starAlgHom_ext fun v => by rw [StarAlgHom.comp_apply, hf, hg]; rfl
  · exact h₂.starAlgHom_ext fun v => by rw [StarAlgHom.comp_apply, hg, hf]; rfl

/-- A C⋆-envelope `κ : V → E` is onto when `V` is unitally completely order isomorphic to a unital
C⋆-algebra `A`, in any universe: the ⋆-homomorphism `π : A → E` of the universal property
(`OperatorSystem.IsCStarEnvelope.exists_surjective_starAlgHom`) is onto, so `κ = π ∘ j` is onto. -/
lemma surjective_of_surjective (hκ : IsCStarEnvelope κ) {A : Type*} [CStarAlgebra A]
    [PartialOrder A] [StarOrderedRing A] {j : V →ₗ[ℂ] A} (hj : j.IsCompleteOrderEmbedding)
    (hj1 : j 1 = 1) (hsurj : Function.Surjective j) : Function.Surjective κ := by
  have hgen : (StarAlgebra.adjoin ℂ (Set.range j)).topologicalClosure = ⊤ := by
    refine eq_top_iff.mpr fun a _ => StarSubalgebra.le_topologicalClosure _ ?_
    exact StarAlgebra.subset_adjoin ℂ _ (hsurj.range_eq ▸ Set.mem_univ a)
  obtain ⟨π, hπ, hπj⟩ := hκ.exists_surjective_starAlgHom j hj hj1 hgen
  intro y
  obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ := hπ y
  obtain ⟨v, rfl⟩ := hsurj a
  exact ⟨v, (hπj v).symm⟩

/-- A C⋆-envelope of `V` is one of every operator system `V'` unitally completely order isomorphic
to `V`, along the isomorphism. -/
lemma comp {V' : Type*} [AddCommGroup V'] [Module ℂ V'] [StarAddMonoid V'] [StarModule ℂ V']
    [PartialOrder V'] [∀ k, PartialOrder (CStarMatrix (Fin k) (Fin k) V')] [One V'] [OperatorSystem V']
    (hκ : IsCStarEnvelope κ) (e : V' ≃ₗ[ℂ] V) (he : (e : V' →ₗ[ℂ] V).IsCompleteOrderEmbedding)
    (he1 : e 1 = 1) : IsCStarEnvelope (κ ∘ₗ (e : V' →ₗ[ℂ] V)) where
  map_one := by rw [LinearMap.comp_apply, LinearEquiv.coe_coe, he1, hκ.map_one]
  isCompleteOrderEmbedding := hκ.isCompleteOrderEmbedding.comp he
  topologicalClosure_adjoin_range := by
    rw [LinearMap.coe_comp, Set.range_comp, LinearEquiv.coe_coe, e.surjective.range_eq, Set.image_univ]
    exact hκ.topologicalClosure_adjoin_range
  exists_starAlgHom A _ _ _ j hj hj1 hgen := by
    have he1' : e.symm 1 = 1 := e.symm_apply_eq.mpr he1.symm
    obtain ⟨π, -, hπj⟩ := hκ.exists_surjective_starAlgHom (j ∘ₗ (e.symm : V →ₗ[ℂ] V'))
      (hj.comp he.symm) (by rw [LinearMap.comp_apply, LinearEquiv.coe_coe, he1', hj1]) (by
        rwa [LinearMap.coe_comp, Set.range_comp, LinearEquiv.coe_coe, e.symm.surjective.range_eq,
          Set.image_univ])
    refine ⟨π, fun v => ?_⟩
    have h := hπj (e v)
    rwa [LinearMap.comp_apply, LinearEquiv.coe_coe, e.symm_apply_apply] at h

end IsCStarEnvelope

/-- **The operator systems that come from unital C⋆-algebras are exactly those that coincide with
their C⋆-envelope.** A C⋆-envelope `κ : V → E` is onto if and only if `V` is unitally completely
order isomorphic to a unital C⋆-algebra `A`. If `κ` is onto, so is the embedding of `V` into
`OperatorSystem.CStarEnvelope V`, which is ⋆-isomorphic to `E` over `V`
(`OperatorSystem.IsCStarEnvelope.exists_starAlgEquiv`), and it is such an `A`; conversely `κ` is onto
(`OperatorSystem.IsCStarEnvelope.surjective_of_surjective`, for `A` in any universe). The `iff`
quantifies `A` over the universe of `V`, which contains `OperatorSystem.CStarEnvelope V`. -/
theorem IsCStarEnvelope.surjective_iff {V : Type u} [AddCommGroup V] [Module ℂ V] [StarAddMonoid V]
    [StarModule ℂ V] [PartialOrder V] [∀ k, PartialOrder (CStarMatrix (Fin k) (Fin k) V)] [One V]
    [OperatorSystem V] {E : Type*} [CStarAlgebra E] [PartialOrder E] [StarOrderedRing E]
    {κ : V →ₗ[ℂ] E} (hκ : IsCStarEnvelope κ) :
    Function.Surjective κ ↔
      ∃ (A : Type u) (_instA : CStarAlgebra A) (_instPO : PartialOrder A)
        (_instSOR : StarOrderedRing A) (j : V →ₗ[ℂ] A),
        j.IsCompleteOrderEmbedding ∧ j 1 = 1 ∧ Function.Surjective j := by
  refine ⟨fun h => ?_, fun ⟨_, _, _, _, _, hj, hj1, hsurj⟩ => hκ.surjective_of_surjective hj hj1 hsurj⟩
  have h₀ := isCStarEnvelope_toCStarEnvelope V
  obtain ⟨e, he⟩ := hκ.exists_starAlgEquiv h₀
  refine ⟨CStarEnvelope V, inferInstance, inferInstance, inferInstance, toCStarEnvelope V,
    h₀.isCompleteOrderEmbedding, h₀.map_one, fun y => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨v, hv⟩ := h (e.symm y)
  exact ⟨v, by rw [← he, hv, StarAlgEquiv.apply_symm_apply]⟩

end OperatorSystem
